+
+class RasterSourcePattern(:class:`Pattern`)
+============================================
+
+.. class:: RasterSourcePattern(content, width, height)
+
+    :param cairo.Content content: the content type of the pattern
+    :param int width: the width of the raster source pattern
+    :param int height: the height of the raster source pattern
+    :raises Error:
+    :rtype: RasterSourcePattern
+
+    Create a new raster source pattern.
+
+    A raster source pattern is a user pattern providing raster data. It is
+    useful for implementing patterns which are more complex than gradients
+    or simple surfaces, for example when the pixel data needs to be
+    generated on demand.
+
+    The pattern is driven through a set of callbacks which are set with
+    :meth:`set_acquire`, :meth:`set_snapshot`, :meth:`set_copy` and
+    :meth:`set_finish`.
+
+    .. method:: set_acquire(acquire, release)
+
+        :param callable acquire: the acquire callback
+        :param callable release: the release callback
+
+        Sets the acquire and release callbacks of the pattern.
+
+        The acquire callback is called with ``(pattern, target, extents)``
+        and should return a :class:`Surface` providing the pixel data for
+        the region of interest described by ``extents``.
+
+        The release callback is called with ``(pattern, surface)`` once the
+        pixel data is no longer being accessed and should typically finish
+        or destroy the surface created by the acquire callback.
+
+    .. method:: get_acquire()
+
+        :returns: a tuple of (acquire, release) callbacks
+        :rtype: tuple
+
+        Gets the currently set acquire and release callbacks.
+
+    .. method:: set_snapshot(snapshot)
+
+        :param callable snapshot: the snapshot callback
+
+        Sets the snapshot callback of the pattern. It is called with
+        ``(pattern)`` and should return a :class:`cairo.Status`.
+
+    .. method:: get_snapshot()
+
+        :returns: the snapshot callback or :obj:`None`
+        :rtype: callable or None
+
+        Gets the currently set snapshot callback.
+
+    .. method:: set_copy(copy)
+
